Tai-e, a whole-program static taint analyzer, is run on this project with exactly the inputs below: the entry program it starts from and its taint policy files (Tai-e YAML: sources introduce attacker-controlled data, sinks are the dangerous arguments, transfers propagate taint between values). You receive the same configuration the analyzer receives.

Entry program `PlexusUtilsEntry.java` (the analysis starts at its `main` method):
```java
import java.io.File;
import org.codehaus.plexus.util.Expand;

/** Analysis entry point only: the benchmark runner never executes this class. */
public class PlexusUtilsEntry {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        Expand expand = new Expand();
        expand.setSrc(new File("analysis-input.zip"));
        expand.setDest(new File("analysis-output"));
        expand.execute();
    }
}
```

